														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2059833">
									

<p>I think this is fantastic. I want to know so much more, which is always a good sign.</p>
<p>I do have one suggestion, though. Calling the people in the logs &quot;Subject A&quot; and &quot;Subject B&quot; carries with it some subtle implications that you probably don't intend. It makes it seem as if they were the only two people fully observed, or like they were somehow connected (like they were being tested for two different outcomes or something). It's a little hard to explain the kind of subtle connotations that terms can have, so I hope I'm communicating it well enough. The bottom line is, I would probably change them to something along the lines of &quot;Subject 2055-17&quot; and &quot;Subject 2055-38.&quot;</p>
<p>Either way, +1</p>

							</div>

								
					
