<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Best practice in relation to SCP-2055 is currently limited to constant monitoring of key personnel and the suppression of public knowledge.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be a 'the' in front of the sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the event of automated monitors being triggered the nearest available security officers should be alerted and authorised to carry out immediate physical intervention.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be a comma between triggered and the. Authorised is spelled Authorized.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In cases where remote monitoring has allowed SCP-2055 to be interrupted, affected individuals have become highly agitated and resistant.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't need to be in the containment procedures.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once removed from the location of onset, abnormal behaviours cease, with the individual exhibiting no memory of preceding events.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ditto this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Due to the difficulty in predicting the occurrence, prevalence or individual outcomes of SCP-2055, constant surveillance is currently the only certain counter-measure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This has already been stated as the first line in the containment procedures.</p>
