				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/litfried" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1391439); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1391439&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607439577" alt="Litfried" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1391439)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/litfried" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1391439); return false;" >Litfried</a></span> <span class="odate time_1404233054 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Jul 2014 16:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2061722">
									

<p>I'd like to lay in my opinions against Soulless' here and say that</p>
<p>a) 'Best practice' is <em>definitely</em> correct and 'the best practice' is incorrect in this instance - they have subtly different meanings and should be used in slightly different contexts</p>
<p>b) A comma is not necessary where you have indicated, and 'authorised' is a perfectly legitimate spelling of the word</p>
<p>c) Methods of dealing with affected individuals are very much part of containment when the SCP is a phenomenon which affects large numbers of people</p>
<p>d) Agree with you about the redundancy in your penultimate point</p>
<p>e) I don't really think collapsing the logs is necessary. They're such an integral part of the piece. I think collapsing them will (incorrectly) project that all-too-familiar <em>twist incoming</em> feeling.</p>

							</div>

								
					
